# SDLC — Docs as source of truth (project has docs hub)

When the project has a **docs** folder used as SDLC (e.g. **docs/index.md** with a Plan / Done / WIP / Backlog section):

1. **Use docs as the authority** for what is in scope, what is done, and what is next. Before implementing, check docs/index.md and the linked spec docs.

2. **After implementing or changing scope**, update the docs hub (usually docs/index.md):
   - Add or move completed work under Done / implemented.
   - Add or move in-progress work under WIP with correct tags.
   - Keep Backlog and any “backlog by category” in sync.

3. **Keep specs and code aligned.** If code diverges from a spec in docs, either update the code to match the spec or update the spec and note the change.

4. **Entry point:** The main doc (e.g. docs/index.md) is the single place to see current state and which spec to follow. Keep its Plan section and tags up to date when shipping or changing features.

This rule applies when working in or with files under **docs/** so that implementation stays tracked and reflected in the project’s SDLC docs.
